# ListGroup, ListRow

> Lede 0.7.0's docs for ListGroup, ListRow, installed with it. Setup, and every item in the release: [README.md](README.md). Online: https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/list.md

ListGroup is a `<section>` with a heading and a `<ul>` of ListRows. A ListRow is a link, a button, a static row or a row that opens its details, with leading and trailing slots and up to three actions in a ••• menu and a touch swipe, where a disabled action shows its reason.

## Install

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add @lede/list @lede/switch
```

The command needs Lede's registry in `components.json`, as [README.md](README.md#use-it-in-a-shadcn-project) shows. It also installs the items [`lede-theme`](lede-theme.md), [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md) and [`theme-provider`](theme-provider.md), and the npm packages `@base-ui/react@^1.9.0` and `@react-aria/interactions@^3.28.1`. It adds [`switch`](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/switch.md) only because the example below imports it. The item's JSON, with each file's source, is https://lede.cloudcompute.com/r/v0.7.0/list.json.

## Import

```tsx
import { ListGroup, ListRow } from '@/components/lede/list';
```

## Files and exports

| Installs to | Import from | Exports |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `components/lede/list.tsx` | `@/components/lede/list` | `ListGroup` (component), `RowActionItems` (component), `ListRow` (component), `ListGroupProps` (type), `RowAction` (type), `ListRowProps` (type) |

## ListGroup props

A `<section>`, a heading and a `<ul>`. The heading names the section for assistive tech.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `title` | `React.ReactNode` |  | The group's heading: a real heading, `<h2>` by default, that names the section. |
| `summary` | `React.ReactNode` |  | The group's one-line takeaway beside the heading, such as "2 on" or "All up to date". It moves under the heading when the two don't fit. |
| `footer` | `React.ReactNode` |  |  |
| `empty` | `React.ReactNode` |  | Shown in place of the rows when there are none, such as "No hosts match" under a filter. Without it, a group with no rows still shows its empty list. |
| `headingLevel` | `2 \| 3 \| 4 \| 5 \| 6` | `2` | Heading level for `title`. Default 2. |
| `children` | `React.ReactNode` |  | ListRow elements. |
| `className` | `string` |  |  |

## ListRow props

An `<li>` whose primary target is a real `<a>` (`href`) or `<button>` (`onClick`). The swipe is a touch and pen shortcut, through React Aria's `useMove`. An action that removes its row moves focus to the next row, else the one before, else the group's heading. A parent that moves focus itself after removing a row does it in a layout effect or inside `flushSync`, so its move comes first and the row leaves it there.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `title` (required) | `React.ReactNode` |  |  |
| `subtitle` | `React.ReactNode` |  |  |
| `subtitleLines` | `1 \| 2 \| 'all'` | `1` | How many lines the subtitle shows before it ends in an ellipsis: 1, 2 or `'all'`. Default 1. |
| `value` | `React.ReactNode` |  | Trailing secondary value, such as "On". |
| `leading` | `React.ReactNode` |  | A 30px leading slot (`--size-leading`): an icon tile (`span.ld-tile`) or an Avatar. It is hidden from assistive tech. |
| `control` | `React.ReactNode` |  | A leading control, such as a selection Checkbox. It is exposed and sits above the row's link target. Beside a Checkbox, the line between rows starts where the title does; another control keeps the leading slot's inset. |
| `trailing` | `React.ReactNode` |  | Trailing control, such as a Switch. Leave `href` and `onClick` unset with it, since interactive elements don't nest. |
| `href` | `string` |  | Navigates: the row renders a real `<a>`. |
